                         alt="Life of a plant image"
                         loading="lazy">
                  </a>


          

      



        <div class="work-details">

<dl>
          
            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Title:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Life of a Plant</span> </dd>
              </div>
            
        


            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Description:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> An acrylic-on-canvas triptych, inspired by different colours of a plant. </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            

            

            

            

            



            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Size:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">20 cm x 20 cm each</span> </dd>
              </div>
            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Medium:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Acrylic on canvas</span> </dd>
              </div>
            



            

            



            

            



            

            




            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Date:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> August 2024 </span> </dd>
              </div>
            

     </dl>

    </div>]]><![CDATA[<p>We have a big pretty plant (of the Scindapsus pictus kind I think). One day, after spotting one of its leaves that had fallen off, I felt inspired to paint something plant-related.</p>







    

    

    

    
        
    

    

    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/paintings/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_leaf.jpg">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/paintings/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_leaf_hu1449941057489291313.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

<p>I found the combination of bright greens in younger leaves, the deep dark greens in mature ones, and the yellowish-brown colour of an occasional dead leaf interesting. Since I had three canvases, I tried painting something resembling three stages of a plant&rsquo;s life.</p>
<p>Getting the colours right took some trial and error.</p>







    

    

    

    

    
        
    

    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/paintings/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_paint_mixing.jpg">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/paintings/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_paint_mixing_hu5531893980789346206.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

<p>Here&rsquo;s one more pic.</p>







    

    

    

    

    

    
        
    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/paintings/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_side.jpg">
