Sun, 04 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>
A personal website created in Hugo.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[

      

          

            

                  

                  
                  
                      
                  

                  
                      
                          
                      
                  


                  


                  <a href="https://tlocrt.com/other/web/tlocrt_website/images/tlocrt_website_202409.png">
                    <img class="work-image"
                         src="https://tlocrt.com/other/web/tlocrt_website/images/tlocrt_website_202409_hu13544187863326975319.png"
                         alt="tlocrt website image"
                         loading="lazy">
                  </a>


          

      



        <div class="work-details">

<dl>
          
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Title:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">tlocrt Website</span> </dd>
              </div>
        


            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Description:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> A personal website created in Hugo. </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            

            

            

            

            



            

            

            



            

            



            

            



            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">URL:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> <a href="https://tlocrt.com/">https://tlocrt.com/</a> </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Date:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> August 2024 </span> </dd>
              </div>
            

     </dl>

    </div>]]><![CDATA[<p>This website was created in <a href="https://gohugo.io/">Hugo</a>. Since I was a web development noob, it took a small eternity. But it was fun!</p>
<p>What you&rsquo;re seeing is a custom Hugo theme, developed by following the first ~1/3 of the helpful book <a href="https://pragprog.com/titles/bhhugo/build-websites-with-hugo/"><em>Build Websites with Hugo</em></a> by Brian P. Hogan and then freestyling (aka typing semi-coherent questions into various search engines and LLMs until something started working).</p>
<h2 id="whats-up-with-the-name">What&rsquo;s up with the name?</h2>
<p>The word &ldquo;tlocrt&rdquo; (pronounced tlotsrt) means &ldquo;ground plan&rdquo; in Serbo-Croatian.
I picked it mainly because I liked how the word looked with its kind-of symmetry.
Also it&rsquo;s not easy to find a cool domain name in 2024 that is also available&hellip;</p>
<p>The logo was inspired by the meaning of the word and contains artistic interpretations of elements of technical drawings.</p>
<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
<p>Features that took way more time than they should have include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Serving a downsized version of all images (unless the user clicks on an image &mdash; then they get all the pixels).</li>
<li>Responsive design (this means that things will be positioned and scaled differently, depending on your screen size).</li>
<li>Automatically generated &ldquo;Latest&rdquo; section on the homepage (the secret sauce was using <code>.Site.RegularPages</code> instead of <code>.Site.Pages</code>).</li>
<li><del>RSS feed</del> not quite ready yet :/</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="todo">TODO</h2>
<p>Every time I work on the website, I get many wonderful ideas of what I can do next, all of which I promptly forget the moment I stop working on it.</p>
<p>Cue: a TODO list.</p>
<ul>
<li><del>Maybe reconsider the font</del> Font was reconsidered!</li>
<li>Make priority lists nicer</li>
<li>Tidy up the css / work details</li>
</ul>
]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Zürich</title><link>https://tlocrt.com/visual/photography/zurich/</link><guid>https://tlocrt.com/visual/photography/zurich/</guid><pubDate>
